utral":0.8,"def_epa_per_play":-0.01677},{"week":17,"opponent":"PIT","home":true,"pf":24.0,"pa":22.0,"off_snaps":61,"epa_per_play":0.1742,"pass_rate":0.5082,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5682,"def_epa_per_play":0.1114}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2022,"team":"TEN","distance":0.6676,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"PIT","distance":0.7105,"shared":15,"play_caller":null},{"season":2019,"team":"LV","distance":0.7539,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2020,"team":"LV","distance":0.7859,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2019,"team":"TEN","distance":0.7909,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2019,"team":"SF","distance":0.3808,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Robert Saleh"},{"season":2021,"team":"SF","distance":0.4099,"shared":18,"play_caller":"DeMeco Ryans"},{"season":2018,"team":"JAX","distance":0.5944,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"SF","distance":0.5945,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2020,"team":"LAC","distance":0.6451,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Browns went 11-5 in 2020 and were outscored 419 to 408. The offense carried the team, ranking 10th in EPA per play while the defense finished 23rd in EPA allowed. What set them apart was the highest 13 personnel usage and the 2nd highest Cover 4 rate in the league.","offense":"The Browns offense was well above average by EPA per play. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Their biggest outliers in how they lined up were the highest 13 personnel usage and the most tight ends on the field in the league. Baker Mayfield ran the passing game, with Jarvis Landry leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Browns defense was well below average by EPA allowed per play. Its strongest area was explosive play rate allowed, where it ranked 9th, and its weakest was EPA allowed per dropback, where it ranked 23rd. Myles Garrett was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Adrian Clayborn, who had 3.5 sacks while playing only 41% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they had the 2nd highest Cover 4 rate in the league.","special":"The Browns were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 79% of field goals, which was well below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into receivers, about 17% of the money on the books. Their tight ends were among the youngest in the league.","players":"Baker Mayfield played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 3,563 yards. Targets were spread around, with Jarvis Landry and Austin Hooper leading a group where nobody took more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield was a committee led by Kareem Hunt and Nick Chubb. On defense, Myles Garrett led the team with 12 sacks and B.J. Goodson picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Kevin Stefanski called the offense, and the defensive play caller for this season is not in the coaching data. Their offense looked most like the 2022 Titans and the 2024 Steelers. Their defense looked most like the 2019 and 2021 49ers.","trends":"The offense went from 22nd in EPA per play in 2019 to 10th in 2020, a big step forward. The defense moved from 20th in EPA allowed per play in 2019 to 23rd in 2020, a modest decline. The biggest change in approach was blitz rate, which went from 38% to 21%.","notes":"FTN did not start charting plays until 2022, so play action, motion, RPO and screen rates are not available for 2020. Everything else, including personnel, formations and coverage, is complete for this season."}}